            "heading": "Our Story",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_pdecwc": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Twenty-five years ago I was getting ready for a party in East Hampton putting on my expensive, American-made jeans and was struck by how the jeans were designed to look rich and worn but were basically very unflattering.  In fact, the \"wear\" pattern on the denim actually made the body look <em>worse</em>: hips wider and legs shorter with wide horizontal lines low on the hip; butt and upper thighs bigger with large white areas accentuating them; pooched-out stomach with waistbands above the natural waist or spill-over with the waistband too low; and the front of the thighs bigger with large white areas smooshed across the thigh!! The back pockets had all these huge logos on them which looked utterly ridiculous.</p>",
            "text_color": "#000000",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_Kq6KDH",
